==============================================================================
What width actually separates the census candidates
==============================================================================

   in hand: c = 0.903 +/- 0.0375  (the epsilon-blind ensemble)

   candidate            value      distance from 9/10   sigma now
   8/9  (charge-weighted, Sum N_c Q^2 = 8) 0.88889   0.01111      0.30
   9/10 (the standing census)             0.90000   0.00000      0.00
   12/13 (the wider roster)               0.92308   0.02308      0.62

   the BINDING spacing is 9/10 vs 8/9 = 0.01111
   (9/10 vs 12/13 = 0.02308, twice as easy)

   the quoted target sigma_c <= 0.0115 buys:
     9/10 vs 8/9   : 0.97 sigma
     9/10 vs 12/13 : 2.01 sigma
   -- i.e. at the quoted width the charge-weighted candidate still
      sits one sigma away. That is not a separation; it is the
      width at which the two stop coinciding.

   what a genuine call costs (binding pair, 9/10 vs 8/9):
     level    sigma_c needed   sharpening vs now   data multiple
     2 sigma      0.00556            6.7x                   46x
     3 sigma      0.00370           10.1x                  103x
     5 sigma      0.00222           16.9x                  285x

VERDICT:
   THE RECORDED CLOSING MOVE DOES NOT CLOSE. sigma_c <= 0.0115 is
   the candidate SPACING, so it delivers a 1.0-sigma separation
   from the charge-weighted alternative — the alternative survives
   comfortably at that width. A 3-sigma call needs sigma_c <=
   0.00370, which is a 10.1x sharpening, not 3.3x, and
   because ensemble width falls as 1/sqrt(N) that is ~103x the data,
   not ~11x. The 3.3x figure understates the cost of the closing
   move by an order of magnitude in width and two in sample.

   This does not change c's STATUS — it was already a counting
   assumption the framework does not force, and the ensemble
   already confirms without adjudicating. What changes is the
   cost of the adjudication: it is not nearly in reach, and any
   plan that treats sigma_c = 0.0115 as the finish line is
   planning to stop one sigma short of a decision.
==============================================================================
